# 🖥️ Kiosk Mode Rules

These rules define how to lock down the browser for unattended kiosk deployment.

---

## 1 — `useKioskMode` Hook (`src/hooks/useKioskMode.ts`)

A single hook that suppresses browser behaviours that break the kiosk experience. Called **once** at the app root (e.g., inside the root layout or `_app`).

Must prevent:

| Behaviour           | Technique                                                         |
| ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Right-click menu    | `window.addEventListener("contextmenu", e => e.preventDefault())` |
| Pinch-to-zoom       | Block `touchstart` when `e.touches.length > 1`                    |
| Safari gesture zoom | Block `gesturestart` and `gesturechange`                          |
| Ctrl + scroll zoom  | Block `wheel` when `e.ctrlKey` is true                            |

- All listeners registered in **one** `useEffect` with full cleanup on unmount.
- Touch listeners must use `{ passive: false }` to allow `preventDefault()`.

```ts
export function useKioskMode() {
    useEffect(() => {
        const preventContextMenu = (e: MouseEvent) => e.preventDefault();
        const preventPinchZoom = (e: TouchEvent) => {
            if (e.touches.length > 1) e.preventDefault();
        };
        const preventGestureZoom = (e: Event) => e.preventDefault();
        const preventCtrlScrollZoom = (e: WheelEvent) => {
            if (e.ctrlKey) e.preventDefault();
        };

        window.addEventListener("contextmenu", preventContextMenu);
        window.addEventListener("touchstart", preventPinchZoom, { passive: false });
        window.addEventListener("gesturestart", preventGestureZoom, { passive: false });
        window.addEventListener("gesturechange", preventGestureZoom, { passive: false });
        window.addEventListener("wheel", preventCtrlScrollZoom, { passive: false });

        return () => {
            window.removeEventListener("contextmenu", preventContextMenu);
            window.removeEventListener("touchstart", preventPinchZoom);
            window.removeEventListener("gesturestart", preventGestureZoom);
            window.removeEventListener("gesturechange", preventGestureZoom);
            window.removeEventListener("wheel", preventCtrlScrollZoom);
        };
    }, []);
}
```

---

## 2 — Global CSS Lockdown

Applied to `*` (all elements) in the global stylesheet:

```css
* {
    touch-action: manipulation !important;
    user-select: none !important;
}
```

| Property                     | Purpose                                                                       |
| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `touch-action: manipulation` | Allows tap and scroll only; disables double-tap-to-zoom and browser gestures. |
| `user-select: none`          | Prevents text selection across the entire app.                                |

Both use `!important` to override any component-level styles.

